{"id":"4fd1b58efa572dce7c70acd9950f1c32804542eb02abb4a0385c25c26ffe17c7","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:27.785998348Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"Umbrella for six deepening candidates found in the 2026-10-10 architecture review. Each is a sub-issue; none contradicts ADR 0001 or ADR 0002, and candidates 1 and 3 reinforce ADR 0002.\n\n## Sub-issues\n\n1. Ticket history and closed-time behind TicketStore (Strong)\n2. Code Review as a ticgit-lib module (Strong)\n3. Fork-merge (`ti pull`) as a lib operation emitting ops (Strong)\n4. One Search, sort and stats for CLI and TUI (Strong)\n5. Ticket-mutation skeleton and docs/CLI contract test (Worth exploring)\n6. Workflow rules (Claim, Promote, Dependency) gathered in the lib (Worth exploring)\n\n## Suggested order\n\nStart with 3, then 1: both are correctness gaps against ADR 0002 with small, testable scope. The sub-issues are independent of each other; work whichever the frontier offers.\n\n## Not recommended (recorded so they are not re-suggested)\n\n- Splitting the TUI or the store by file alone: adds no depth; candidates 1, 2 and 4 shrink the TUI first.\n- A shared git subprocess adapter: overlaps candidate 2's adapter.\n- The sync hook and sync module: consistent with ADR 0001, leave alone."}}}